From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 13:23:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/47] fix(prompts): stop asserting one Dolt server on 3307 in
 operational-awareness (gcp-o86m)

The operational-awareness fragment is injected into every gastown role card,
and its Dolt section opened by asserting that Dolt "runs as a single server on
port 3307 serving all databases." On hammer that premise is not incomplete, it
is inverted: the city's managed server listens on :51160 and holds hq/th/gcp,
while :3307 is an external server holding only the winnow rig's beads. Verified
this session from gc doctor --json:

  dolt-server                   | ok | reachable on 127.0.0.1:51160
  rig:gascity-packs:dolt-server | ok | inherits city dolt endpoint
  rig:winnow:dolt-server        | ok | reachable on 127.0.0.1:3307

The fragment then prescribed a pre-escalation bundle -- gc dolt sql/logs/health/
status -- all four of which resolve their port from the managed server's
dolt-state.json. So on this topology the documented diagnostic structurally
cannot observe the server whose outage would trigger the escalation. During the
2026-08-12 beads incident two seats produced wrong diagnoses within an hour of
each other while correctly following this text, and one was a step from
escalating catastrophic data loss on evidence describing the wrong server.

The fix is endpoint resolution rather than a different hardcoded port. The
section now: states that a city can run more than one server; tables the three
gc.endpoint_origin values (managed_city / inherited_city / explicit) against
where that scope's beads actually live; tells the reader to resolve the endpoint
from the scope's own .beads/config.yaml BEFORE diagnosing; labels gc dolt * as
managed-server-only; and adds the corollary that an empty database on the
managed server whose name matches an externally-pinned rig is evidence you
queried the wrong server, never evidence of data loss. A new bundle step 5 runs
gc doctor, whose per-rig rig:<name>:dolt-server probe dials each rig's own
resolved host:port and is the only documented check that reaches an external
endpoint. The stop/start and SIGQUIT paths are scoped to the managed server,
since an externally-pinned server is not gc-supervised.

Validation: both documented snippets run verbatim -- the .beads/config.yaml grep
reproduces the winnow (explicit, 127.0.0.1:3307) vs gascity-packs
(inherited_city) split, and the jq filter produces the three-line output quoted
above. The template parses and executes under text/template with .CityRoot bound,
leaving no unrendered actions. go build/vet, go test -race, golangci-lint (0
issues) and validate_registry.py are green.

Deliberately out of scope, tracked in gc-tmla against the gc binary: making
gc dolt status/health print or disclaim the endpoint they report on, and the
recurring auto-created empty database named after an externally-pinned rig.
Separately filed gcp-ha55 for a pre-existing tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py
failure on gastown/tests/test_merge_approval_gate.sh, reproduced with this
change stashed.
